                                        "entry_id": "509306c1-222b-375d-ad99-f1f1c6eb7107",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Controlled distribution of scarce resources such as food or fuel; used typically in wartime."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3daf4dc6-b0b4-44e9-a4c6-e2e7dee68629",
                                                "sense_id": "8aa3856a-01de-3924-921a-900b0c7652cd",
                                                "text": "The drastic rationing of paper enforced by the paper control, has made it necessary for us to adapt ourselves to the altered conditions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bca30640-f6fc-4c06-9f4c-a3bb662282de",
                                                "sense_id": "8aa3856a-01de-3924-921a-900b0c7652cd",
                                                "text": "After petrol rationing ended in 1952, the BTC was aware that more swingeing cuts had to be made, and a sinister message was conveyed by the loss of the meandering 38-mile route from Blisworth to Stratford-upon-Avon in April 1952, and the 25-mile Abergavenny-Merthyr Heads of the Valleys line in January 1958."
                                            }
